127
00:08:12,883 --> 00:08:13,601
Go back:

128
00:08:15,367 --> 00:08:16,903
Let me try something.

129
00:08:16,903 --> 00:08:22,171
Delete a branch with unmerged work, a different way of "losing" commits:

130
00:08:22,733 --> 00:08:24,978
Deleted branch risky (was ...):

131
00:08:24,978 --> 00:08:27,224
Git even printed the commit ID.

132
00:08:27,224 --> 00:08:35,118
If the terminal output is gone, the reflog still has the commit, as the last position of HEAD on that branch:

133
00:08:36,867 --> 00:08:38,666
Here is the fix.

134
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:41,113
Got it.

135
00:08:41,113 --> 00:08:43,865
What do I need to remember?

136
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:48,520
The reflog records every move of HEAD and branches in your clone.

137
00:08:49,067 --> 00:08:54,891
HEAD@{N} / branch@{N} name those old positions; reset or branch to them.

138
00:08:55,433 --> 00:08:58,986
It is local and expires (90 days by default):

139
00:08:58,986 --> 00:09:03,328
recover soon, and it never replaces pushing or backups.
